# Build context filter for docker/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile; a docker/.dockerignore
# would be ignored since the context is the repo root).
#
# A developer clone carries the outputs of host builds (autotools files
# generated by another autoconf/libtool, objects and libtool archives built
# for another OS or architecture, a core dump). The image regenerates and
# rebuilds everything from source, so none of that may reach the context:
# stale objects newer than their sources would be linked as is. The list
# mirrors the build-output part of .gitignore; dockerignore patterns are
# anchored at the context root, hence the **/ prefixes for nested outputs.

# VCS, editors, packaging and this folder: not inputs of the build
.git
.githooks
.github
.ruby-lsp
.vscode
debian
docker
core

# Autotools output at the root (regenerated by autoreconf -f -i)
aclocal.m4
autom4te.cache
compile
config.*
configure
configure~
depcomp
install-sh
libtool
ltmain.sh
m4/*.m4
missing
stamp-h?
test-driver

# Build output anywhere in the tree (**/ also matches the root)
**/Makefile
**/Makefile.in
**/.deps
**/.libs
**/.dirstamp
**/*.o
**/*.lo
**/*.la
**/*.a
**/*.so
**/*.so.*
**/*.log
**/*.trs
src/monikor
tests/check_libmonikor
